<br/>
<i>If you're struggling with mana then it's fine to leave the Spirit -&gt; Crit reforges off your gear. They are very small changes. If you're not planning on moving immediately to raids then it's also ok to wear all four pieces of tier (leave out Gloves) since the 4pc-bonus is slightly stronger in easier content.</i>
<h5 class="heading-size-5" id="where-to-get-gear">Where to get gear</h5>You'll get most of your pre-raid gear from a few specific sources:<ul>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Elemental Rune Protocol: Twilight dungeons <b>(New in Phase 4)</b>:  This is a higher difficulty of dungeon content that drops a very wide range of 384 gear along with <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=3281/obsidian-fragment">
<span>
<img alt="Obsidian Fragment" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_stone_15.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Obsidian Fragment</span></span></a>. It will make up the majority of your pre-raid gear unless you're already well equipped from phase 3.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=3281/obsidian-fragment">
<span>
<img alt="Obsidian Fragment" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_stone_15.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Obsidian Fragment</span></span></a> <b>(New in Phase 4)</b>: Kind of entwined with the above but the currency dropped from the dungeons lets you buy 384 item level Dragon Soul tier pieces, special effect items and more!</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=396/valor-points">
<span>
<img alt="Valor Points" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/pvecurrency-valor.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Valor Points</span></span></a>: A limited currency that'll have a higher cap every week. Valor items are 397 and the highest you can get without stepping foot into Dragon Soul. Early on you'll use Valor to fill key slots with few to no alternatives. Later on you can use it to increase your overall item level if you don't plan on raiding or if you've been unlucky in a few slots.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=395/justice-points">
<span>
<img alt="Justice Points" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/pvecurrency-justice.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Justice Points</span></span></a>: A more entry level currency that you can use to buy lower item level gear. If your character is new then it's very useful for putting together a set good enough to do higher dungeon difficulties. Justice is also a dungeon drop.</div></li></ul>
<h5 class="heading-size-5" id="priority-stats">Priority Stats</h5>We'll be eyeing the following on our Pre-BiS pieces, while continuing to prioritize item level:<ol>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<b>Intellect:</b> Offers spell power, mana, crit and regeneration. An absurdly strong stat.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<b>Haste Rating:</b> Our best secondary stat regardless of playstyle.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<b>Spirit</b>: Spirit is particularly valuable when undergeared since your mana regeneration before you get a lot of intellect is extremely poor.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<b>Critical Strike</b>: Similar in value to Spirit. While gearing don't worry too much whether your piece has crit or spirit on it. Either is fine.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<b>Mastery:</b> An unfortunately weak stat.</div></li></ol>You will want to socket <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=52207/brilliant-inferno-ruby">
<img alt="Brilliant Inferno Ruby" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_cutgemsuperior6.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Brilliant Inferno Ruby</span></a> gems in the majority of your sockets regardless of color unless the socket bonus is worth 20 or more intellect per non-red gem.<h2 class="heading-size-2" id="cataclysm-currencies">Cataclysm Currencies</h2>
<div class="clear"></div>
<div class="tabs-wrapper">
<div id="dsf67g4d-currencies">
<div class="tabs-container">
<ul class="tabs" role="tablist">
<li data-first-in-row="true" data-selected="true" role="tab">
<a href="#currencies-justice-points" rel="np" tabindex="-1">
<div>
<span class="icontiny lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/small/pvecurrency-justice.jpg");'></span>Justice Points</div>
<b>
<span class="icontiny lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/pvecurrency-justice.gif");'></span>Justice Points</b></a></li>
<li data-first-in-row="false" role="tab">
<a href="#currencies-valor-points" rel="np">
<div>
<span class="icontiny lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/small/pvecurrency-valor.jpg");'></span>Valor Points</div>
<b>
<span class="icontiny lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/pvecurrency-valor.gif");'></span>Valor Points</b></a></li>
<li data-first-in-row="false" role="tab">
<a href="#currencies-obsidian-fragments" rel="np">
<div>
<span class="icontiny lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/small/inv_stone_15.jpg");'></span>Obsidian Fragments</div>
<b>
<span class="icontiny lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_stone_15.gif");'></span>Obsidian Fragments</b></a></li>
<div class="vertical-scroll-shadow"></div>
<div class="horizontal-scroll-shadow"></div></ul></div></div>
<div class="tabbed-contents">
<div id="tab-currencies-justice-points" style="">
<h3 class="heading-size-3 first" id="justice-points-for-discipline-priest-healer-pre-raid">Justice Points for Discipline Priest Healer Pre-Raid</h3>You can get <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=395/justice-points">
<span>
<img alt="Justice Points" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/pvecurrency-justice.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Justice Points</span></span></a> by killing bosses in Heroic Dungeons and completing Random Dungeons through the Random Dungeon Finder tool.<br/>
<br/>You can spend them at the following Justice Point Vendors:<ul>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a data-entity="npc" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/npc=46555/gunra">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Gunra</span></a> (Horde)</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a data-entity="npc" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/npc=44246/magatha-silverton">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Magatha Silverton</span></a> (Alliance)</div></li></ul>Phase 2 items that previously cost <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=396/valor-points">
<span>
<img alt="Valor Points" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/pvecurrency-valor.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Valor Points</span></span></a> are now purchasable using <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=395/justice-points">
<span>
<img alt="Justice Points" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/pvecurrency-justice.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Justice Points</span></span></a>. These are all catch up or starter pieces now so you don't have to worry as much about what order you buy them in. You aren't going to use any of these items for very long and you'll replace everything as you continue to gear. Consider prioritizing the 378 items - particularly <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=71211/soothing-brimstone-circle">
<img alt="Soothing Brimstone Circle" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_ring_firelandsraid_02c.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Soothing Brimstone Circle</span></a> since it's well itemized and will let you spend your more premium currencies on other slots but there are no wrong answers in regards to what you buy.<br/>
<br/>
